From: OpenWrt
Subject: [PATCH] mdns_mdnssd: fix ServiceInstanceResolution fd/object leak

ServiceSubscription::Resolve() pushes a new ServiceInstanceResolution
onto mResolvingInstances on every "add" browse event, with no check
for a stale prior resolution of the same instance already present.
ServiceInstanceResolution::FinishResolution() -- called once a
resolution completes -- never erases `this` from mResolvingInstances
and never deallocates its DNSServiceGetAddrInfo ref (the second-phase
DNSServiceRef; the first-phase DNSServiceResolve ref is already
correctly deallocated in HandleResolveResult() before this point).

Since browse "add" events recur every time a service instance's mDNS
cache entry refreshes (observed here via a border router repeatedly
rediscovering its own _trel._udp advertisement roughly every 6-7
minutes -- normal mDNS TTL-refresh behavior), mResolvingInstances
grows without bound and leaks one otbr-agent<->mdnsd UNIX socket per
still-browsed interface on every such cycle. On this OpenWrt/duo-ap
setup that is 6 interfaces, i.e. 6 leaked file descriptors per event,
eventually exhausting the process's fd table and crashing otbr-agent
(otPlatInfraIfHasAddress() ... No file descriptors available).

Fix: before invoking any callback that could free the owning
ServiceSubscription (see the existing NOTE below), move `this` out of
mResolvingInstances into a local unique_ptr so the object stays alive
for the remainder of this function, then erase the (moved-from) slot
from the vector. When the local unique_ptr goes out of scope at the
end of the function, ~ServiceRef() -> Release() -> DeallocateServiceRef()
runs as already implemented, correctly closing the leaked ref instead
of leaking it forever. This mirrors the existing move-then-erase
pattern already used by Publisher::RemoveServiceRegistration() in
mdns.cpp for the same self-destruction hazard.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/mdns/mdns_mdnssd.cpp
+++ b/src/mdns/mdns_mdnssd.cpp
@@ -1316,6 +1316,26 @@
     std::string            serviceName  = mSubscription->mType;
     DiscoveredInstanceInfo instanceInfo = mInstanceInfo;
 
+    // Move `this` out of `mResolvingInstances` before calling `OnServiceResolved` below
+    // (which may free `subscription`, per the existing NOTE) so that this resolution's
+    // DNSServiceGetAddrInfo ref gets deallocated via ~ServiceRef() once `self` goes out
+    // of scope, instead of leaking forever: without this, a new "add" browse event for
+    // the same instance (e.g. this BR periodically rediscovering its own _trel._udp
+    // record as its mDNS cache entry refreshes) pushes another ServiceInstanceResolution
+    // onto mResolvingInstances on top of this now-orphaned one -- one leaked fd per
+    // still-browsed interface, every such cycle.
+    auto &instances = subscription->mResolvingInstances;
+    auto  it        = std::find_if(instances.begin(), instances.end(),
+                                   [this](const std::unique_ptr<ServiceInstanceResolution> &aInstance) {
+                                       return aInstance.get() == this;
+                                   });
+    std::unique_ptr<ServiceInstanceResolution> self;
+    if (it != instances.end())
+    {
+        self = std::move(*it);
+        instances.erase(it);
+    }
+
     // NOTE: The `ServiceSubscription` object may be freed in `OnServiceResolved`.
     subscription->mPublisher.OnServiceResolved(serviceName, instanceInfo);
 }
